romdev-core-bsnes
=================

wasm/bsnes_libretro.wasm and wasm/bsnes_libretro.js are built from bsnes
(https://github.com/libretro/bsnes, the libretro port of bsnes by byuu / Near
and contributors) at the commit pinned in romdevtools/scripts/versions.json
(cores.bsnes), with romdev's patch (romdevtools/scripts/patches/
bsnes-romdev.patch and patches/bsnes/).

bsnes is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
(GPL-3.0-only; the full text is GPLv3.txt in the bsnes source). libco and nall,
which bsnes includes, are under the ISC license. The built core is therefore
distributed under GPL-3.0; its corresponding source is the pinned bsnes commit
plus the romdev patch and build script named above.

Code transplanted from bsnes elsewhere in romdev: the recompiler's SNES chip
units (romdevtools/src/analysis/recompile/wat/snes/bsnes-chips.json, built by
romdevtools/scripts/recompile-gen/bsnes-chips.mjs) are bsnes's uPD96050 and
ARM coprocessor code, and romdev's snes9x core build links the same code
(romdevtools/scripts/patches/snes9x-bsnes-chips.patch). Those files are
GPL-3.0, and a recompiled cart or core that contains them is GPL-3.0 too.

No coprocessor firmware is included. The ST010/ST011/ST018 firmware is not
part of bsnes or romdev; a user supplies it.
